{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-01e37d63-ed88-45c9-a47f-01e463f483f5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-84d3613a68496a47","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9019-9zickyud/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9019-E001.md","content":"# Tutorial packaging format and validation tooling\n\n## Description\n\nDefines the tutorial packaging format that decouples tutorial content from\nDashboard releases, plus the tooling that validates a packaged tutorial against\nit. The format is the contract that both the Dashboard tutorial gallery (which\nreads tutorial metadata and launches pinned images) and authored tutorial\ncontent (which is packaged, versioned, and tested in the format) build against.\nThis epic's priority is P0 by priority inheritance: it directly gates both P0\nrequirements of the strategy (the gallery launch mechanics and the curated\ntutorial suite).\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define the tutorial packaging format: a metadata descriptor per tutorial\n  (identity, covered journey, tutorial kind — notebook or pipeline), pinned\n  container images, and a validation manifest.\n- Define the versioning scheme that lets a tutorial package be released and\n  updated independently of Dashboard releases.\n- Provide validation tooling that mechanically checks a packaged tutorial\n  conforms to the format (metadata completeness, image pinning, manifest\n  present and consistent).\n- The format spans Dashboard, Notebooks, and Data Science Pipelines surfaces;\n  this epic is assigned to the Dashboard component because the gallery is the\n  primary consumer, and is owned by the Dashboard team with review from the\n  Workbenches and Pipelines teams as the other format consumers.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The format specification documents the metadata fields, image pinning rules,\n  and validation manifest structure.\n- A tutorial packaged in the format can be validated mechanically with a\n  pass/fail result by the validation tooling.\n- A versioned tutorial package can be updated to a new version without\n  requiring a Dashboard release.\n- The format specification is reviewed and agreed by the Dashboard, Workbenches,\n  and Pipelines teams (all three consuming teams).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1): a tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation\n  manifest) is defined so tutorials are versioned and testable independently of\n  Dashboard releases. Epic priority is P0 by inheritance — this format gates\n  the P0 gallery and P0 tutorial suite work.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":35356,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-825fc3402b7e8127","agent_id":"a8883c02dfbae495e","session_id":"8e8f3f7e-9881-4ba0-8b86-168f23b1e6dd","uuid":"536a00a5-bdec-4c27-9ca0-e559ba9145c6","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:04:57.661Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9019"}
