{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ea64a5841d3e5d3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# RHAISTRAT-9019 Decomposition — Curated getting-started tutorial gallery\n11\t\n12\tTriage (Step 0): the strategy is not below-threshold and not docs-only. Its own\n13\tproblem statement identifies three architecturally distinct work streams with\n14\tdifferent owners and review processes — product code (gallery + launch\n15\tmechanics in the Dashboard), authored content (the tutorials themselves), and\n16\tdocumentation — spanning four components and at least three teams. The\n17\tmultiple-distinct-work-streams escape condition applies, so a full\n18\tdecomposition was produced.\n19\t\n20\tTeam assignments were inferred from the architecture-context owning teams\n21\t(`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/`), because the strategy\n22\tcontains no Impacted Teams table — see Health Warnings.\n23\t\n24\t## Epic List\n25\t\n26\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n27\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Tutorial packaging format and validation tooling | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Dashboard tutorial gallery and one-click launch | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n30\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 | Curated notebook tutorial suite | Implementation | Workbenches | P0 |\n31\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | First-pipeline tutorial | Implementation | RHOAI Pipelines | P0 |\n32\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | Tutorial gallery documentation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n33\t\n34\t## Dependency DAG\n35\t\n36\t```mermaid\n37\tgraph TD\n38\t  E001[RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 packaging format] --> E002[RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 gallery + launch]\n39\t  E001 --> E003[RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 notebook tutorials]\n40\t  E001 --> E004[RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 pipeline tutorial]\n41\t  E001 --> E005[RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 documentation]\n42\t  E002 --> E005\n43\t  E003 --> E005\n44\t  E004 --> E005\n45\t```\n46\t\n47\t## DAG Justification\n48\t\n49\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n50\t|------|------|-----------|\n51\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) is the contract the gallery's code parses and launches from; the gallery builds against it. |\n52\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | Notebook tutorials are packaged and validated in the format; content authors build against it. |\n53\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The pipeline tutorial is packaged and validated in the same format. |\n54\t| E001, E002, E003, E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | The docs-authoring epic is blocked by every Implementation epic in the strategy; docs describe what was built. These edges do not trigger priority inheritance (docs-authoring priority exception). |\n55\t| no edge: E002 ∥ E003, E002 ∥ E004 | Rule 14 (independent repos/artifacts) | Gallery code and tutorial content live in different repos owned by different teams. HLR-3 exists precisely so tutorials are versioned and testable independently of Dashboard releases; the gallery is verified against format-conformant tutorial packages, not against the authored suite. |\n56\t| no edge: E003 ∥ E004 | Rule 1 / Rule 14 | Different components and different owning teams (Workbenches vs RHOAI Pipelines); no shared artifacts beyond the format both consume from E001. |\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n59\t\n60\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n61\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n62\t| HLR-1 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Gallery surface and one-click launch mechanics (workbench with notebook, pipeline import). |\n63\t| HLR-2 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E003, RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Split along the component/team boundary (Rule 1): the five notebook-journey tutorials (Workbenches) and the first-pipeline tutorial (RHOAI Pipelines) are separate epics because different teams author and review them; together they cover all six journeys, each tested against the current release. |\n64\t| HLR-3 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Priority inheritance: raised to P0 because it directly gates both P0 HLRs (HLR-1 and HLR-2). The P1 label reads as relative value, not deferral — the format is a prerequisite, not deferrable. |\n65\t| HLR-4 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | docs-authoring priority exception: strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1 (not P2, and does not push priority upstream). |\n66\t\n67\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n68\t\n69\t## Health Warnings\n70\t\n71\t- **Missing strategy sections** (proceeded with available information): the\n72\t  strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies table, no\n73\t  Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, no Non-Functional Requirements, and no\n74\t  effort estimate. Team assignments were inferred from the architecture-context\n75\t  owning teams (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard; Notebooks → Workbenches; Data\n76\t  Science Pipelines → RHOAI Pipelines). The documentation epic's owner\n77\t  (\"RHOAI Documentation\") is inferred — no context file covers the\n78\t  Documentation component; confirm with PM.\n79\t- **Priority inversion (non-blocking)**: HLR-3 is P1 but its epic gates all P0\n80\t  work and is raised to P0 by priority inheritance. If product decides the\n81\t  gallery can ship against a draft format, the E001 → E002 edge could be\n82\t  relaxed; as specified, the format is a hard prerequisite.\n83\t- **Scope trap / ongoing maintenance commitment**: HLR-2's \"tested against the\n84\t  current release\" implies a per-release regression pass over all six\n85\t  tutorials. Initial delivery is covered by E003/E004 acceptance criteria, but\n86\t  no epic owns the re-test cadence beyond this release — recommend a\n87\t  follow-up maintenance agreement.\n88\t- **Component mapping notes** (non-obvious mappings): E001's format spans\n89\t  Dashboard, Notebooks, and Data Science Pipelines; assigned the single\n90\t  canonical component `Dashboard` because the gallery is the primary consumer.\n91\t  E003's tutorials exercise workbench, training, serving, and RAG surfaces;\n92\t  assigned `Notebooks` as the most-relevant canonical component (the tutorials\n93\t  are notebook content running on workbenches).\n94\t- **Passive components**: Notebooks and Data Science Pipelines need no code\n95\t  changes — tutorials use the existing workbench lifecycle and pipeline import\n96\t  surfaces. Their validation is captured as acceptance criteria on E003 and\n97\t  E004 respectively (same owning team validates), not as separate validation\n98\t  epics.\n99\t\n100\t## Tiered Delivery\n101\t\n102\tNot applicable — the strategy has no external dependencies with uncertain\n103\ttiming (Dependencies table absent, Open Questions: None); all work is\n104\tin-platform.\n105\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e582ab3f6005988","agent_id":"a8756bfc8c6f3dfa6","session_id":"8e8f3f7e-9881-4ba0-8b86-168f23b1e6dd","uuid":"48142169-7963-4e0e-b53e-d3a6529de86e","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:07:29.777Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ea64a5841d3e5d3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
